    "title": "Report on Cook County Election Procedures",
    "text": "• The author has served as an election judge in Cook County, Illinois, multiple times.\n• Election materials are delivered to the Cook County Board of Elections collection point.\n• Tabulation tapes are checked at the collection point.\n• Tabulation tapes require the signatures of the election judges.\n• If the tapes lack the required signatures, they are not accepted.\n• The Cook County Sheriff's Police have been dispatched to locate election judges to sign the tapes.\n• The author implies that the actions of those involved give the appearance of corruption.",
